              "title": "The best Boardwise alternatives",
              "kind": "comparison",
              "markdown": "Looking for an alternative to Boardwise? These are the tools teams most often compare it with, ranked by how many of the criteria that matter to most buyers they meet, with what each is best for.\n\n## Our verdict\n\nThere is no single best alternative to Boardwise: the right one depends on whether you need timelines, a free plan, or the lowest price. Read the one-line reasons below, then check the matrix against your own list.\n\n## Why teams switch\n\nThe usual reasons to leave Boardwise are cost at scale, a feature held back for a higher plan, or a tool that no longer fits how the team works.\n\n## How to switch\n\n1. Export your data from Boardwise.\n2. Import it into the alternative you picked and check the mapping.\n3. Move one project first, then the rest.\n\n## Frequently asked questions\n\n### What is the best free alternative to Boardwise?\n\nThe free-plan row of the matrix shows which of these have one.\n\n### Is it hard to switch from Boardwise?\n\nProjects and tasks move by CSV in a few minutes; automations have to be recreated by hand.\n\n## How we compared\n\nFacts come from each vendor's own documentation, with sources and dates shown. The ranking follows the number of key criteria each tool meets, not a score we award.\n",
